# FIXED 2026-08-26 (the spread application rework: an operator
# arriving as a peer-only key is CARRIED, never wrapped as a frozen
# expectation -- handleExpectedVal / the pcIsOp guard in go/mapval.go).
# Claim C6 (use-case 02 gap 4): an expression whose operand references
# back into the pack-generated subtree could not be merged onto the
# generated child -- the wrap froze the op and the residue blamed a
# spread that existed nowhere ([aontu/mapval_spread_required]). The
# carried op now keeps computing and resolves against the generated
# child once the pack fires: surge is 3. The failure was never
# pack-specific -- `a:{x:1} a:{y:.x+1}` died the same way and works
# now too (plus.tsv peer-key-expr); an op that can NEVER resolve is an
# honest error naming the real path (plus.tsv
# peer-key-expr-unresolvable). Pinned in the shared spec: gen-pack.tsv
# pack-merge-expr-onto-child.
# expected: {"deploy":{"web":{"replicas":2,"surge":3}}}
# actual:   {"deploy":{"web":{"replicas":2,"surge":3}},"names":["web"]} exit 0
names: [web]
deploy: pack($.names, { replicas: 2 })
deploy: web: { surge: $.deploy.web.replicas + 1 }
